Use a list when:

"I have multiple items and I care about the collection/order of those items." ->

servers = ["web-01", "web-02", "db-01", "redis-01"]

ordered -> yes
duplicates -> yes
mutable -> yes
access by -> index

-------

Use a tuple when:

"These values belong together, and I don't want this collection modified."

ordered -> yes
duplicates -> yes
mutable -> no
access by -> index

--------
sets : "I only care whether something exists"

    - No duplicates
    - Sets are also great for membership

ordered -> no*
duplicates -> no
mutable -> yes
access by -> membership

#------
dictionary : "I want to associate a value with a name"

ordered -> yes
duplicates -> keys:no
mutable -> yes
access by -> key
